  <tr> 
    <td valign="top" align="center"> 
      <table width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="3" height="5611">
        <tr> 
          <td height="2"> 
            <div align="center">&nbsp;</div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="718"> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Wu-Fu 
              Chen </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/Wu-Fu-Chen.jpg" width="72" height="70" align="right"></font><font color="#000099"><br>
              <br>
              </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Biography 
              of </font></b></font><font color="#000099">Wu-Fu Chen <br>
              </font></b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Wu-Fu 
              Chen </i></b>is a Partner of Acorn Campus, Genesis Campus and Crimson 
              Ventures. He is the co-founder of fourteen companies involved in 
              Optical, Multi-services, Enhanced services, Semiconductor, Wireless, 
              and New Data Center Infrastructure technologies. He is currently 
              the Chairman of Anda Networks, Cinta Corporation, Santera Systems, 
              Optimight Communications, Navini Networks, New Tone Communications 
              and 3UP Systems, and is a board member of Axon Communications, Pine 
              Photonics, Polaris Networks, Rapid Stream, vWeb and Zettacom.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Wu-Fu 
              </i></b>is best known for his role as founder and V.P. of Engineering 
              at Cascade Communications. He helped Cascade become a worldwide 
              leader in the frame relay market for service providers with $500 
              million in sales, leading up to its 1994 IPO and its 1997 sale to 
              Ascend, now Lucent. Wu Fu also founded Communications Equipment 
              Corporation (acquired by AT&amp;T/Paradyne in 1989), Arris Networks 
              (acquired by Cascade in 1996), Ardent Communications (purchased 
              by Cisco in 1997) and Shasta Networks (acquired by Nortel in 1999). 
              </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Wu-Fu</i></b> 
              has been ranked as the most influential person in optical networking 
              by Light Reading magazine and was elected as one of the top ten 
              entrepreneurs of 2000 by Red Herring magazine. He was previously 
              V.P. of Technologies at Cisco Systems, where he was responsible 
              for leading Cisco's MC3810 Integrated Voice, Data &amp; Video Access 
              Concentrator product development team. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Wu-Fu 
              </i></b>started his career with product development and staff scientist 
              positions at Bytex and Wang Laboratories before founding Communications 
              Equipment Corporation. He holds an MSEE degree from the University 
              of Florida at Gainesville and a BSEE degree from the National Taiwan 
              University.</font></p>
            <p></p>
            <p></p>
            <p></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="876"> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#000099"><b>Chin-Cheng 
              Wu</b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/Chin-Cheng-Wu.jpg" width="72" height="100" align="right"><br>
              Chairman<br>
              Acopia Networks Inc.<br>
              <br>
              <b><font color="#000099">Biography of Chin-Cheng Wu</font></b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><br>
              <b><i>Mr. Wu</i></b> became Chairmanof Acopia Networks in December, 
              2001 after leaving Cisco Systems. Acopia Networks is a development 
              stage company focusing on next generation storage networking products.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Mr. Wu 
              </i></b>joined Cisco Systems in June 2000 - through Cisco's acquisition 
              of ArrowPoint Communications for $5.7B. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Since he joined 
              Cisco, Mr. Wu has assumed various executive positions.<br>
              Prior to becoming VP of Strategy, Mr. Wu headed up Cisco's Content 
              and Multiservice Edge Group (CME) as Group VP and General Manager. 
              CME group's technology focus is to enable the migration of existing 
              client-server multi-protocol networks toward high value, multiservice 
              (data, voice, and video) architectures capable of supporting the 
              next wave of e-business applications and edge services for Enterprise 
              and SP customers.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Mr. Wu's responsibilities 
              as group vice president include, setting and influencing the CME 
              group's technical direction, communicating technology information 
              to and mentoring senior staff, as well as spreading the CME group's 
              technology vision through the company and the industry.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Prior to joining 
              Cisco, he was ArrowPoint Communications' founder, chairman of the 
              board, and chief executive officer. Founded in 1997, ArrowPoint 
              provided Web switches and Web network services (WebNS?) software 
              that allowed customers to optimize the use of the Web for e-commerce 
              and content delivery.<br>
              <br>
              Preceding Mr. Wu's time with ArrowPoint, he served as Cascade (now 
              Lucent Technologies) Communications' vice president for remote access 
              engineering, and co-founded Arris Networks, a Massachusetts based 
              startup that developed high-density Internet access products. Arris 
              was founded in October, 1995 by Mr. Wu and Mr. Wufu Chen; it was 
              sold to Cascade for $150M in May, 1996, only 7 months into founding.<br>
              <br>
              To highlight his career in the networking and communications industry 
              - which extends more than 20 years -Mr. Wu's was named to InteractiveWeek 
              Magazine's &quot;Top 25 Unsung Heroes of the Internet&quot; list 
              in 2000.<br>
              <br>
              <b><i>Mr. Wu</i></b> has a bachelor's degree in electrical engineering 
              from ChiaoTung University, Tiawan (1972, BS), and a master's degree 
              in computer science from Indiana University in 1977.<br>
              </font></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="417"> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Jenny 
              Chen</font><i></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/jennychen.jpg" width="72" height="91" align="right"><b><i><br>
              <br>
              </i><font color="#000099">Biography of </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#000099">Jenny 
              Chen</font></b></font> <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i><br>
              Jenny Chen</i></b> was one of NECINA founding member in 1996 and 
              happy volunteer in this non-profit organization for 6 years. She 
              is currently severed as NECINA Board of Director and General Manager. 
              </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Jenny</i></b> 
              graduated from Beijing University of Aeronautics &amp; Astronaut, 
              with B.S. in Computer Engineering and was a UN visiting scholar 
              studied at WANG Laboratory. Jenny received Master's degree of Computer 
              Science from Rivier College, New Hampshire in May 1992.</font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Over the ten 
              years, Jenny has been working at US network and telecommunication 
              companies such as FiberNet Research Inc., Cabletron Systems, Cascade 
              Communication, Lucent Technologies, and Unisphere Networks etc. in position of the Senior Networking Embed System &amp; NMS testing engineer, Pre-sale technical support, Marketing Manager in China, as well as Senior Staff member at Unisphere Networks in  Westford, MA Since Jan. 2000.
            .<br>
              </font></p>
            </i>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="249"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Dick 
            Chiu</font><i></i></b></font><br>
            <font color="#000099"><br>
            Biography of </font></b></font><font color="#000099">Dick Chiu</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/images/dick.jpg" width="81" height="92" align="right"><b><i><br>
            Dick Chiu </i></b>is NECINA's president and one of the first founding 
            members who initiated the creation of NECINA and has been a board 
            director since its inception. Dick is the Director of Software Engineering 
            at Appian Communications and is responsible for the development of 
            its network management system. Prior to Appian, he was a Sr. Manager 
            at Cascade Communications and at Ascend Communications with similar 
            responsibility. He would like to foster start-up companies in telecommunication 
            and networking industries. Dick holds a BS in Electrophysics and MBA 
            from Chiao Tung University, and MS in Computer Engineering from Syracuse 
            University. <br>
            </font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="477"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Thomas 
            W. Huang</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/THUANG.jpg" width="72" height="91" align="right"><b><i><br>
            <br>
            </i><font color="#000099">Biography of Thomas W. Huang</font></b></font> 
            <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i></i></b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i><br>
            Thomas W. Huang </i></b>is a Partner at the Business Law Department 
            of Holland &amp; Knight, LLP where he practices primarily in the areas 
            of general business law, financing and international transactions. 
            He is also the Responsible Partner of the Taiwan Practice Group of 
            the firm. </font> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">In conjunction 
              with his practice, he has been a frequent speaker at seminars and 
              conferences sponsored by bar associations, CLE programs, universities 
              and law schools. He has also authored many publications, particularly 
              in the areas connected with doing business in China. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Mr. Huang</i></b> 
              is a member and has served on many civic and business organizations. 
              He served on the steering committee of the International Law Committee 
              of the Boston Bar Association for nearly ten years and was a member 
              of the Massachusetts Governor's Advisory Council on Guangdong, China, 
              for many years. He is one of the founders and the clerk/director 
              of the Asian American Bank &amp; Trust Company in Boston. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Mr. Huang 
              </i></b>was born in Taipei, Taiwan (China) and obtained his LL.B. 
              degree from National Taiwan University. He subsequently obtained 
              a J.D. magna cum laude from Indiana University Law School and an 
              LL.M. and an S.J.D. degree, both from Harvard Law School.<br>
              </font></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="306"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">David 
            W. Sung</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/sung.jpg" width="72" height="93" align="right"><b><i><br>
            <br>
            </i><font color="#000099">Biography of David W. Sung</font><i><br>
            David W. Sung</i></b> is a partner at CommonwealthCapital. Dave has 
            12 years of operational, entrepreneurial and venture capital experience 
            in networking and communications. Dave is currently a director or 
            observer of Kenetec Systems, Paceline Systems, Crossbeam Systems and 
            Ivivity. Before joining Commonwealth Capital, Dave was a Co-Founder 
            and CEO of Crescent Networks and a Co-Founder of Cadia Networks. Dave 
            also held engineering, marketing and executive management positions 
            at Cascade Communications, Avici Systems, FORE Systems and Bytex Corp. 
            Dave received his BSEE at Northeastern University and has done graduate 
            work at Boston University.<br>
            David W. SungPartner<br>
            <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20020706095451if_/mailto:dsung@commonwealthvc.com">dsung@commonwealthvc.com</a></font> 
            <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"> <br>
            </font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="496"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Edward 
            L.W. Soong</font></b></font> <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><br>
            <b><br>
            <font color="#000099">Biography of</font><font color="#000099"> Edward 
            L.W. Soong</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/images/edsoong.jpg" width="80" height="96" align="right"><b><i><br>
            CV SUMMARY</b></font> <br>
            <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Ed </i></b>has 
            spent over 32 years in engineering, management, sales, and marketing 
            in the Electronics, Information Technology, and e-Commerce industries. 
            Ed is the founder and President of Anew Technology Corporation in 
            Burlington, Mass. The company's focus is in e-Commerce Systems Development 
            business since 1995. Previously, Ed worked in Wang Laboratories, Inc. 
            for 17 years. His last position was the Senior Director of Business 
            Development in Wang's Asia &amp; Pacific Operations.</font> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Ed</i></b> 
              has been active in community services. He was the president of Great 
              Boston Chinese Cultural Association, Director of the Board of Monte 
              Jade Science and Technology Association, and co-founder and president 
              of New England Chinese Information and Networking Association (NECINA). 
              Currently, he serves on the board of NECINA, New England Association 
              of Chinese Professionals, and Chinese Economic Development Council 
              in Boston Chinatown.<br>
              <br>
              <i><b>Ed</b></i> graduated from Chiao Tung University in Hsinchu, 
              Taiwan with a B.S. in Electronic Engineering. He also holds a M.E. 
              in Electrical Engineering, a M.S. in Computer Science, and a M.B.A. 
              He is an author of a Prentice Hall technology book - &quot;Fundamentals 
              of Web Applications using .NET and XML&quot;. Ed loves outdoor activities 
              and plays competitive soccer year round. <br>
              </font></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="382"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#000099"><b>Jo 
            Tango</b></font> <font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/tango.jpg" width="72" height="83" align="right"></font> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Biography 
              of</font><font color="#000099"> </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#000099"><b>Jo 
              Tango</b></font></b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><br>
              </b></font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Jo</i></b> 
              is a General Partner focused on information technology investments. 
              His current investment interests are distributed computing and storage 
              infrastructure. Jo represents Highland on the boards of Beliefnet, 
              BondEra and Touchpoint, and has been actively involved with Ask 
              Jeeves, NextCard, Be Free, Digital Market and LivePerson.<br>
              <br>
              </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Before 
              joining Highland, Jo spent five years with Bain &amp; Company, where 
              he focused on high-growth initiatives and infrastructure projects. 
              While with Bain, he worked on a new strategy for America Online's 
              network services business, which resulted in the AOL/Compuserve/Worldcom 
              transaction. He also worked extensively with AT&amp;T on its long-distance 
              business, as well as on international expansion projects with American 
              Express and Royal Ahold.<br>
              <br>
              </font><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Jo's other 
              experiences include working in mergers and acquisitions at Wasserstein 
              Perella, in later-stage private equity at Bain Capital. He has a 
              B.A. from Yale University and an M.B.A. from the Harvard Business 
              School.<br>
              </font></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="325"> 
            <p align="left"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Charlie 
              Qing Wang</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/charlie.jpg" width="72" height="93" align="right"><b><i><font color="#0000CC"><br>
              <br>
              </font></i><font color="#000099">Biography of </font><font color="#000099">Charlie 
              Qing Wang</font><i><font color="#0000CC"></font></i></b><i><b><br>
              Mr. Charlie Qing Wang</b></i> has more than 10 years of telecom 
              and data communications industry experience, ranging from product 
              design and development, system engineering, to technical marketing 
              and product management and product marketing for SONET/SDH, metro 
              DWDM, optical Ethernet and data networking companies (Nortel Networks, 
              Lucent Technologies and local startup companies). He specializes 
              in marketing and product-managing optical networking, SONET and 
              SDH, DWDM and optical Ethernet and Data networking products. Most 
              recently, Mr. Wang served as a Sr. Product Manager at METRObility 
              Optical Systems of Merrimack, NH, an optical Ethernet company. Mr. 
              Wang serves as a Director, Board of Directors of NECINA. Mr. Wang 
              has a M.A.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from Simon Fraser University, 
              Canada and a B. Eng. from Beijing Institute of Technology (BIT) 
              in Beijing, China.<br>
              </font></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="363"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Hong 
            Yu</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/hongyu.jpg" width="72" height="93" align="right"><b><i><br>
            <br>
            </i><font color="#000099">Biography of Hong Yu</font><i><br>
            Hong Yu</i></b>, Founder and ChairmanMr. Yu has been the chairman 
            of the board and chief executive officer of the company since its 
            incorporation in 1996. He also served as president of this 'INC 500' 
            company through June 1998. In 1981, Mr. Yu founded his first entrepreneurial 
            venture, CASAT Technology, a company that developed communications 
            devices for the cable satellite market. Prior to CASAT, his background 
            was in the development of satellite and terrestrial microwave communication 
            systems for the systems and applications division of M/A-Com Corporation, 
            where he held a senior engineering management position. In 1998, Mr. 
            Yu was named &quot;Entrepreneur of the Year&quot; by the both the 
            New Hampshire High Technology Council and the Government of Taiwan 
            and was named &quot;National Minority Small Business Person of the 
            Year&quot; by the US Small Business Administration. He holds 5 patents 
            issued for innovative communications solutions. Mr. Yu holds a BS 
            in Electrical Engineering and an MBA degree, both from the University 
            of Texas.<br>
            </font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="21"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#FF9966">############################################################</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top" height="570"><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><font color="#000099">Dr. 
            Yin</font></b><img src="/web/20020706095451im_/http://www.necina.org/img/team/nanying.jpg" width="72" height="93" align="right"><b></b><br>
            <br>
            <b><font color="#000099">Biography of Dr. Yin</font></b><br>
            As Co-founder and Executive VP of PhotonEx Corporation, <i><b>Dr. 
            Yin</b></i> leads the engineering design and development, product 
            management, SQA and technical documentation for PhotonEx' photonic 
            backbone product. <br>
            <br>
            From 1997-1999, <i><b>Dr. Yin</b></i> was Director of Nortel Networks' 
            Internet Core Router Group, where he initiated and led the development 
            of Nortel's carrier-class core router products, as well as the second-generation 
            IP Packet Processor, the RSPII. From 1995-1997, he served as a Founding 
            Director and Director of Networking Technology of the Bay Architecture 
            Lab, where he led the advanced engineering development of new packet-switching 
            and IP-packet-forwarding components as well as traffic-management 
            mechanisms for new internetworking products. As a Consulting Engineer 
            for Wellfleet Communications and later Bay Networks, Dr. Yin was involved 
            in various projects developing high-end router products from 1993-1995. 
            </font> 
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Dr. Yin</i></b> 
              started his product development career as a Principal Engineer at 
              Motorola, where he focused on techniques for packetized voice and 
              data integration and traffic/bandwidth management. He was also a 
              member of the team that developed Motorola's Frame Relay and ATM 
              switch product. </font></p>
            <p><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><b><i>Dr. Yin</i></b> 
              has published over 20 technical articles and currently holds 20 
              U.S. patents with additional patent applications pending. Dr. Yin 
              received a B.S. from Beijing Shifan University and his M.S., M.Phil. 
              and Ph.D. degrees in Electrical Engineering, Columbia University, 
              New York. </font></p>
            <p></p>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <br>
    </td>
  </tr>
